WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.032 --> 00:00:08.579
One night in July 1916, a fiery blast shook the earth below Ohio’s Lake Erie and trapped

2
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.563
workers in a deep tunnel. Rescuers hurried to the scene, but they were quickly stopped by thick,

3
00:00:13.564 --> 00:00:20.221
choking smoke. The city of Cleveland seemed unprepared to handle the disaster&#8212;many thought the trapped men were

4
00:00:20.222 --> 00:00:26.780
doomed. By the next morning, however, the workers had been rescued, thanks to a breathing device invented

5
00:00:26.781 --> 00:00:32.399
by Garrett Morgan. An African American, Morgan faced many disadvantages because of the color of his skin.

6
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:40.048
Yet his love of mechanical things led him to become an inventor. Where he saw a need,

7
00:00:40.049 --> 00:00:45.254
he worked hard to address it. Morgan’s creativity and persistence made him a hero on that fateful

8
00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:54.908
July night. Garrett Augustus Morgan was born on March 4, 1877, in Paris, Kentucky, the seventh of

9
00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:59.410
11 children born to former slaves. The family was poor, and Garrett left school after sixth grade.

10
00:00:59.411 --> 00:01:08.689
At the time there were few opportunities available to young African Americans, so Garrett spent much of

11
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:14.808
his boyhood working in the fields of the family farm. At the age of 14, he left

12
00:01:14.809 --> 00:01:18.843
home and traveled alone to Cincinnati, Ohio, to find work. He was soon hired as a handyman

13
00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:23.288
by a wealthy white landowner. But Morgan knew he was smart enough to be more than a

14
00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:28.393
simple laborer. In search of a better job, Morgan moved to Cleveland, Ohio, in 1895. Shortly after

15
00:01:28.394 --> 00:01:33.496
arriving in Cleveland, Morgan found a job repairing sewing machines. In his spare time, he experimented with

16
00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:38.892
ways to improve these complicated machines. Morgan’s interest in mechanics blossomed into a skill for fixing different

17
00:01:38.893 --> 00:01:48.434
kinds of machinery, and word of his talent spread through Cleveland’s African American community. Eventually he earned

18
00:01:48.435 --> 00:01:52.314
enough money to buy his own home. In 1907 Morgan opened a sewing-machine repair and sales shop.

19
00:01:52.315 --> 00:01:57.084
Two years later he opened a tailoring shop that employed over thirty people to sew coats, suits,

20
00:01:57.085 --> 00:02:04.484
and dresses. A problem with his sewing machines led to his first famous invention. Morgan noticed that

21
00:02:04.485 --> 00:02:08.956
the friction caused by fast-moving sewing needles could burn woolen fabric, ruining the expensive cloth. So he

22
00:02:08.957 --> 00:02:17.068
began experimenting with polish to reduce the friction. Called to dinner one night, Morgan quickly wiped the

23
00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:21.061
polish from his hands on a curly horsehair cloth. When he returned to work, he saw that

24
00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:27.447
the horsehair had straightened. After trying the polishing cream on a neighbor’s wavy-haired dog, Morgan realized he

25
00:02:27.448 --> 00:02:31.780
had invented something that could straighten hair. He started selling G.A. Morgan’s Hair Refining Cream, or relaxer,

26
00:02:31.781 --> 00:02:39.508
as it is known today. The product was popular, and Morgan’s accidental invention soon made him wealthy.

27
00:02:39.509 --> 00:02:46.619
The success of his businesses allowed Morgan to devote most of his time to inventing. In 1914

28
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:52.116
he obtained a patent for one of his most important inventions, a safety hood for firefighters. Realizing

29
00:02:52.117 --> 00:02:57.322
that smoke and heat rise, Morgan had devised a way for firefighters to breathe air from ground

30
00:02:57.323 --> 00:03:04.881
level. His simple hood contained two tubes that merged into one long tube that hung to the

31
00:03:04.882 --> 00:03:12.198
ground. A water-soaked sponge packed into the opening of the tube filtered out heat and soot. Morgan

32
00:03:12.199 --> 00:03:18.644
planned to travel around the country promoting the safety hood, but he knew many people would not

33
00:03:18.645 --> 00:03:24.404
listen to an African American. To attract buyers, a white business partner acted as the salesman,

34
00:03:24.405 --> 00:03:31.905
while Morgan disguised himself as a Native American. The men demonstrated to astonished crowds that "Big Chief

35
00:03:31.906 --> 00:03:39.620
Mason," wearing Morgan’s safety hood, could enter a smoke-filled tent and emerge unharmed twenty minutes later. A

36
00:03:39.621 --> 00:03:50.795
few orders were placed, but the device had yet to find real success. A disaster two hundred

37
00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:55.605
feet below Ohio’s Lake Erie would change all of that. The city of Cleveland faced catastrophe when

38
00:03:55.606 --> 00:04:01.065
workers accidentally caused a natural gas explosion under Lake Erie. Part of a tunnel fell, killing some

39
00:04:01.066 --> 00:04:08.387
workers and trapping others. Rescuers couldn’t reach the workers because of the heat and toxic gases in

40
00:04:08.388 --> 00:04:12.538
the tunnel. Luckily, a firefighter remembered Morgan’s safety hood. Morgan was called to the scene of the

41
00:04:12.539 --> 00:04:21.298
disaster and arrived with four safety hoods. Morgan, his brother, and two other volunteers wore the safety

42
00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:26.354
hoods into the tunnel, rescuing survivors and bringing out the dead. Others soon took over, and by

43
00:04:26.355 --> 00:04:34.518
morning, Morgan’s invention had saved lives. Stories about the remarkable safety hood appeared in newspapers across the

44
00:04:34.519 --> 00:04:39.732
nation, and orders poured in. White rescuers who used the safety hood that terrible night were praised

45
00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:46.738
in the reports and soon received medals for their heroism. Its African American inventor was overlooked, however,

46
00:04:46.739 --> 00:04:54.715
until Cleveland’s African American citizens honored Morgan's achievement. In 1917 they presented him with a gold medal

47
00:04:54.716 --> 00:05:01.993
for his critical role in the rescue. Morgan continued to invent devices that would help others. In

48
00:05:01.994 --> 00:05:07.664
the 1920s automobiles were becoming popular, but since they were expensive, many people still relied on horse-drawn

49
00:05:07.665 --> 00:05:11.338
carriages and bicycles. Morgan was one of the first African Americans in Cleveland to own a car,

50
00:05:11.339 --> 00:05:20.321
and he witnessed a horrible crash between an automobile and a carriage. Although traffic signals had been

51
00:05:20.322 --> 00:05:29.148
in use for some time, most were simple devices that directed traffic to either stop or go.

52
00:05:29.149 --> 00:05:40.342
Morgan wanted to find a way to make the roads safer. In 1923 Morgan patented a three-way

53
00:05:40.343 --> 00:05:48.509
traffic signal that offered stop, go, and all-stop options. His invention enabled pedestrians to cross streets safely

54
00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:59.831
and ensured that traffic coming from one direction cleared an intersection before traffic coming from the other

55
00:05:59.832 --> 00:06:07.727
direction entered it. Garrett Morgan gained success and wealth as an inventor and businessman, but he wanted

56
00:06:07.728 --> 00:06:12.171
other African Americans to succeed too. In 1920 he created a newspaper, the Cleveland Call. The paper

57
00:06:12.172 --> 00:06:17.840
reported on local and national events that were important to the African American community. Eventually renamed the

58
00:06:17.841 --> 00:06:22.925
Call and Post, the newspaper still exists today. Morgan also became treasurer of the Cleveland Association of

59
00:06:22.926 --> 00:06:31.201
Colored Men, a group devoted to attaining equal standing for African Americans. To further this goal, he

60
00:06:31.202 --> 00:06:36.868
ran for a seat on the Cleveland city council in 1931. Morgan was defeated in the election,

61
00:06:36.869 --> 00:06:44.251
but he stayed active in the community, working to create opportunities for African Americans. Garrett Augustus Morgan

62
00:06:44.252 --> 00:06:55.627
died on July 27, 1963. During his life, he faced poverty and racism. Despite those challenges, he

63
00:06:55.628 --> 00:07:01.411
became a wealthy man. His desire to understand how machines worked turned into a remarkable knack for

64
00:07:01.412 --> 00:07:08.006
innovation. This skill helped him change the lives of others, especially the lives of other African Americans

65
00:07:08.007 --> 00:07:13.944
in his community. Working to improve his own life, Garrett Morgan improved the lives of countless others.

